The [4 carat emerald cut diamond ring](/4-carat-emerald-cut-diamond-ring) is the clearest case in this shape for buying lab. A GIA-certified natural 4ct emerald cut starts at [$97,688](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/20429165?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) in current certified market inventory — that's the stone alone. A lab-grown 4ct D-VVS1 costs [$7,737](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29587315?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational), and the complete ring starts at [$8,427](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29587315?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational).

That's $89,951 less for a stone with better grades. The natural carries G-VS1. The lab carries D-VVS1.

At a 4ct emerald cut table measuring approximately 11mm × 8.5mm, those grade differences are real and visible.

This page covers the full natural 4ct price table, every setting with complete ring totals, the lab alternative that rewrites the budget at this size, the 11mm size guide, clarity and color rules for the step-cut, and four buyer scenarios. Stone plus setting equals ring — both costs are in every table.

---

**TL;DR**

- Natural 4ct: [GIA 4.01ct G-VS1 at **$97,688**](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/20429165?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) (stone only)
- Settings: from [$690 petite solitaire](https://www.bluenile.com/jewelry/rings/petite-emerald-cut-solitaire-diamond-ring-in-14k-yellow-gold-by-james-allen-item-311196?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) to [$4,625 platinum bezel](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/bezel-set-emerald-cut-side-stone-diamond-engagement-ring-in-platinum-by-james-allen-item-304637?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)
- Complete natural 4ct ring: from **$98,378** (G-VS1 + petite solitaire)
- Lab 4ct D-VVS1: [IGI 4.00ct at $7,737](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29587315?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) + $690 = **$8,427 complete** — better grades, $89K less
- Lab 4ct D-FL: [IGI 4.00ct at $16,428](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29327214?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) → ring from **$17,118**
- Size: ~11.0mm × 8.5mm — step-cut's hall-of-mirrors is fully established at 4ct
- Clarity: VS1 minimum for natural; VVS1 or better is standard in lab at this price

→ Best value 4ct ring: [IGI 4.00ct D-VVS1 at $7,737](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29587315?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) + [$690 solitaire](https://www.bluenile.com/jewelry/rings/petite-emerald-cut-solitaire-diamond-ring-in-14k-yellow-gold-by-james-allen-item-311196?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) = **$8,427 complete**, if grades and size matter more than origin.

Priority: if natural origin is non-negotiable, the [GIA 4.01ct G-VS1 at $97,688](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/20429165?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) is the only realistic entry point in current certified market data. If grades take priority, the lab D-VVS1 delivers better quality for $89,951 less.

