## 4 Carat Emerald Cut Diamond Ring Price

Natural 4ct emerald cuts are rare. Two stones appear in current certified market inventory, and the price gap between them shows how sharply grade premiums compound at this carat weight. That gap is $163,160 — for the same carat size.

The entry is a [GIA 4.01ct G-VS1 Ideal Cut](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/20429165?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) at [$97,688](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/20429165?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational). The top of the natural 4ct market is a [GIA 4.12ct D-VVS1](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29395591?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) at [$260,848](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29395591?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational). Moving from G-VS1 to D-VVS1 in natural at 4ct costs $163,160 extra.

At this carat weight, each grade step carries a larger price multiplier than at smaller sizes. The same D-VVS1 grade in lab costs [$7,737](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29587315?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) — $253,111 less than the natural D-VVS1 at the same carat weight.

[![4 carat emerald cut diamond ring in white gold solitaire setting](/images/505033_M1_EMR_DIM_wht_0100CT_W_Box4_004_1600X1600.avif)](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings?MetalType=all&Diamonds=Dia&ShapeID=Emerald&a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)

