## Ring Settings for a 4 Carat Emerald Cut Diamond

[![Petite four-prong emerald cut solitaire ring — correct proportions for a 4ct center stone](/images/505031_M1_EMR_DIM_wht_0100CT_W_Box2_004_1600X1600.avif)](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings?MetalType=all&Diamonds=Dia&ShapeID=Emerald&a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)

At 4ct, the stone is the statement. Narrow, clean settings — the solitaire or a slim bezel — are the right proportional match for an 11mm step-cut center stone. Heavy pavé bands or elaborate side-stone settings compete with the center rather than framing it.

For a natural 4ct at $97K+, the bezel offers meaningful corner protection. The rectangular metal rim shields all four corners — the emerald cut's most vulnerable points on an expensive stone worn daily. The [$990 comfort fit bezel](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/comfort-fit-bezel-set-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-14k-white-gold-by-james-allen-item-315709?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) and [$1,310 bezel solitaire](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/bezel-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-14k-white-gold-item-296642?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) are both correct choices at this stone size.

Settings run from [$690](https://www.bluenile.com/jewelry/rings/petite-emerald-cut-solitaire-diamond-ring-in-14k-yellow-gold-by-james-allen-item-311196?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) for a petite four-prong solitaire to [$4,625](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/bezel-set-emerald-cut-side-stone-diamond-engagement-ring-in-platinum-by-james-allen-item-304637?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) for a platinum bezel with emerald cut side stones. At a $97K stone, the difference between a $690 and $4,625 setting is less than a 4% change in total ring cost — choose based on style, not savings.

