The length-to-width ratio matters at 4ct. A 1.28–1.40 L/W ratio reads as the classic emerald cut rectangle. Below 1.25 trends square; above 1.45 looks elongated.

Both natural 4ct stones are GIA-certified — the GIA report includes exact millimeter measurements. Check the L/W ratio on the grading report before committing.

At 11mm, clarity placement has bigger consequences than at smaller sizes. The table is wider, light paths are longer, and the step facets are more expansive.

A VS2 inclusion that sits safely at the stone's perimeter at 2ct is proportionally closer to the visual center at 4ct. VS1 stays safely eye-clean; anything below requires careful HD video review.

---

## Lab-Grown 4 Carat Emerald Cut Diamond Ring

[![Lab emerald cut diamond ring in rose gold — 4ct D-VVS1 at $7,737](/images/505132_M1_EMR_DIM_wht_0100CT_R_Box4_004_1600X1600.avif)](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings?MetalType=all&Diamonds=Dia&ShapeID=Emerald&a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)

Three lab-grown 4ct emerald cuts are available in current certified market inventory. All three carry grades that the natural 4ct market can't match at these prices: D-VVS1 at the entry, D-FL at the top.

The entry lab stone is an [IGI 4.00ct D-VVS1 Excellent Cut](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29587315?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) at [$7,737](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29587315?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational). D color is the absolute colorless standard. VVS1 means virtually no inclusions visible under 10x magnification. Add the [$690 solitaire](https://www.bluenile.com/jewelry/rings/petite-emerald-cut-solitaire-diamond-ring-in-14k-yellow-gold-by-james-allen-item-311196?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) and the complete ring is $8,427.

The top tier is D-FL — two stones at [$16,428](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29327214?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) and [$17,315](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29273334?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational). Flawless on an IGI lab certificate means internally flawless — not a marketing term. The D-FL at [$16,428](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29327214?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) is 15.9x cheaper than the natural D-VVS1 at [$260,848](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29395591?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational).

